# RUN:   %t/rc.req.json > %t/oracle.skeleton.json %}
# RUN: %if uv %{ diff %t/zkc.skeleton.json %t/oracle.skeleton.json %}

# A bound prices a passage from what the reduction consumes to what it
# produces, so the two must be about the same objects. The contract states
# that directly: each consumed anchor must equal the material filling the
# role of the same name, which is what the produced anchors have been
# constructor-derived from all along. An artifact whose inclusion is about
# columns the round never saw is refused at seal, before any rule reads it.
# RUN: not zkc-opt %pir-seal-full %S/Inputs/logup-unanchored-inclusion.mlir 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LOOSE
# LOOSE: [zkc-E325] an admitted material-identity constraint does not hold
#
# The tie is stated in three places, each saying what it knows. The rule
# requires that every consumed anchor has one, because a bound between two
# claims about different objects prices nothing. The contract says which role
# each anchor is tied to, because that correspondence is its own naming. The
# seal checks the tie holds of this artifact. Drop the contract's half and the
# rule refuses rather than pricing a passage the contract never constrained.
# RUN: %python -c "import json,sys; d=json.load(open(sys.argv[1])); d['reduction_contracts']['logup_range_check']['constraints']=[]; json.dump(d, open(sys.argv[2],'w'))" %zkc-registry-dir/protocol-vocabulary.json %t/untied.vocab.json
