# RUN:   --construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json \
# RUN:   --request=%t/mult.comp.json -o=/dev/null %t/mult.mlirbc 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=COMPMULT
# COMPMULT: condition_failed at apply.conditions.S3

# The condition that keeps a commitment from being priced as a field element,
# in the family where it is the only thing standing there. A value profile may
# be named anything an author likes — including exactly what a payload class
# is called — so a condition comparing the member's declared string against a
# class must be able to tell a profile from a class. Reading the string alone
# bought an evaluation-opening round of commitments a bound of one over the
# field, for values each standing for a million field elements.
